  "synonym_discrimination": {
    "words": [
      "crash-n",
      "accident-n",
      "collision-n"
    ],
    "note": "**Accident** is the general word for something bad that happens without anyone meaning it to, on the road, at home, or at work (*an accident in the kitchen*). **Crash** is an accident in which a vehicle hits something hard, and it suggests force (*a plane crash*). **Collision** is more formal and is used when two moving things hit each other (*a collision between two trucks*)."
